  "description": "Subject: EiffelActivityFinishedEvent \u2013 a1b2c3d4-e5f6-1234-89ab-cdef01234567 (Version 1.1.0)\n\nDear Team,\n\nI\u2019m pleased to inform you that the activity identified by **a1b2c3d4-e5f6-1234-89ab-cdef01234567** has completed successfully. This event, of type **EiffelActivityFinishedEvent**, was recorded at epoch milliseconds **1718451234567** and is tagged with **ci** and **build**. The event originated from our CI/CD domain **com.example.cicd**, specifically from host **build-agent-01.example.com** running **Jenkins** (URI: http://jenkins.example.com/). The serializer used for this event is the **eiffel-serializer** library (group\u202fID: com.example, artifact\u202fID: eiffel-serializer, version\u202f2.3.1). For security, the SDM information records the author as **ci-system@example.com** with the encrypted digest **YmFzZTY0ZW5jb2RlZGRpZ2VzdA==**.\n\nThe outcome of the activity is **SUCCESSFUL** with the description \u201cActivity completed without errors.\u201d A persistent log named **build-log** is available at http://example.com/logs/build.log. Additional custom data captured includes **triggeredBy: git push** and **durationSeconds: 452**. For reference, this event links back to its cause **d3f4e5a6-b7c8-1a2b-9abc-456789abcd12** (type\u202fCAUSE) and provides contextual information **f9e8d7c6-b5a4-3210-9f8e-7654321abcde** (type\u202fCONTEXT).\n\nBest regards,  \nCI System Notification",
